.gradle-user-home/
.gradle/The root issue is that you are accidentally trying to commit your **Gradle cache directory** (`.gradle-user-home/`) to Git.

Dependency cache files should never be committed to source control. In this case, deep directory nesting combined with long package names exceeded the Windows default maximum path length (`MAX_PATH`, 260 characters), causing `Filename too long`.

**1. Ignore the Gradle cache in `.gitignore`**

Add the following lines to your project's `.gitignore` file (create the file in the project root if it does not exist):

```gitignore
.gradle/
.gradle-user-home/
build/
**/build/